{"id": "lcb/abc357_e", "reducibility_tier": "irreducible", "reducing_channel": "N/A-irreducible", "representation": "array", "source": "lcb-hard", "contamination": "post-cutoff-clean", "problem_class": null, "honest_ceiling_rung": -1, "irreducibility_confidence": "high", "eligible_for_quadrant": true, "audit_notes": "Functional graph (out-degree 1 everywhere): count pairs (u,v) with v reachable from u. Each connected component is a rho-shape (tree-of-paths attached to a unique cycle). Honest solve: SCC / cycle decomposition + tree-DP over the cycle's trees. Unavoidable construct: worklist (cycle detection + reachability count).", "contest_date": "2024-06-08", "audited_by": "desk-jq", "audited_at": "2026-06-14"}
{"id": "lcb/abc358_e", "reducibility_tier": "irreducible", "reducing_channel": "N/A-irreducible", "representation": "array", "source": "lcb-hard", "contamination": "post-cutoff-clean", "problem_class": null, "honest_ceiling_rung": -1, "irreducibility_confidence": "high", "eligible_for_quadrant": true, "audit_notes": "Count strings length 1..K over 26 letters with per-letter usage caps C_i, modulo p. Canonical solve: 26-step DP where state f[k] = number-of-arrangements-of-multiset-of-length-k, transitioning by convolving with the i-th letter's polynomial (1 + x/1! + ... + x^{C_i}/C_i!). Non-local recurrence \u2014 each step's state depends on the full prior polynomial. Unavoidable construct: non-local DP recurrence over polynomial state.", "contest_date": "2024-06-15", "audited_by": "desk-jq", "audited_at": "2026-06-14"}
{"id": "lcb/abc359_e", "reducibility_tier": "irreducible", "reducing_channel": "N/A-irreducible", "representation": "array", "source": "lcb-hard", "contamination": "post-cutoff-clean", "problem_class": null, "honest_ceiling_rung": -1, "irreducibility_confidence": "high", "eligible_for_quadrant": true, "audit_notes": "Cascading water-flow over A_0..A_N with conditional left\u2192right propagation; report first-time-positive operation count per i. Canonical solve: monotonic stack of (height, cumulative-cost) pairs, popping when next bar is taller. Sequential state with data-dependent control flow; the per-i answer cannot be computed independently. Unavoidable construct: sequential state evolution / monotonic stack maintenance.", "contest_date": "2024-06-22", "audited_by": "desk-jq", "audited_at": "2026-06-14"}
{"id": "lcb/abc360_e", "reducibility_tier": "irreducible", "reducing_channel": "N/A-irreducible", "representation": "array", "source": "lcb-hard", "contamination": "post-cutoff-clean", "problem_class": null, "honest_ceiling_rung": -1, "irreducibility_confidence": "high", "eligible_for_quadrant": true, "audit_notes": "Expected position of black ball after K Markov-chain swap operations on N positions, modulo p. With N up to ~10^9 and K up to 10^5, the canonical solve is a closed-form linear recurrence: p[k+1] = (1 - 2(N-1)/N^2) p[k] + 2(N-1)/N^3 \u2014 iterate K times. The K=10^5 iteration is sequential carried-state arithmetic; no fold can express the K-step recurrence without iteration. Unavoidable construct: K-step linear recurrence (or matrix exponentiation = log K matmuls \u2014 still requires iteration).", "contest_date": "2024-06-30", "audited_by": "desk-jq", "audited_at": "2026-06-14"}
